additional option to build your iOS project using your Team ID and then perform code-signing on your macOS device. For more information, see iOS Builds  The iOS builds now support only devices with software versions iOS 17 and higher. To learn more, see iOS Builds.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-12\nValid as Of: 2025-02-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1432 ---\nComponent: Variant Configuration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configurations API –Exclude Globally Assigned Characteristics Properly from Configuration Results\nDescription: For a few scenarios in which the characteristics are assigned at different levels in the class hierarchy, and overwritten at more special levels, the response filtered those characteristics although they were assigned to classes. This issue has been corrected.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-10\nValid as Of: 2025-02-12\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1433 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Authorizations Based оn Policies\nDescription: As of February 11, 2025, the MANAGE_USERS policy will no longer contain the read applications permission.  Action: If your scenario requires this permission, you must add the READ_APPLICATIONS policy to the user or users that need it. See how to do this at Configure Application Authorizations | SAP Help Portal.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-01-14\nValid as Of: 2025-02-11\nVersion: 27268\n\n--- Record 1434 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Authorizations Based оn Policies\nDescription: As of February 11, 2025, the MANAGE_USERS policy no longer contains the read applications permission.  Action: If your scenario requires this permission, you must add the READ_APPLICATIONS policy to the user or users that need it. See how to do this at Configure Application Authorizations | SAP Help Portal.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 2025-02-11\nVersion: 27419\n\n--- Record 1435 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Central store logs\nDescription: Central store logs are introduced to provide information about the application-specific groups provisioned from the Identity Directory to target systems.  For more information, see Monitor Central Store Logs.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 2025-02-11\nVersion: 27419\n\n--- Record 1436 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Disabling ID Token Hints for Corporate Identity Providers During Logout\nDescription: Corporate identity providers sometimes have trouble when the ID token is included as a URL parameter in logout requests. With this release, you can disable the inclusion of the URL parameter.  For more information, see Disable ID Token Hints for Corporate Identity Providers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 2025-02-11\nVersion: 27419\n\n--- Record 1437 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Enforce Nonces for Authentication Requests to Corporate Identity Providers\nDescription: Some corporate identity providers require that applications send nonces in their authentication requests. You can enable the service to generate nonces if applications don't provide them.  For more information, Enforce Nonces for Corporate Identity Providers.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 2025-02-11\nVersion: 27419\n\n--- Record 1438 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Group mapping changes\nDescription: The default transformations of SAP Ariba Central Invoice Management, SAP Sales Cloud and SAP Service Cloud, Microsoft Entra ID, and SAP Application Server ABAP are changed to support the provisioning of application-specific groups.  For more information, refer to the relevant connector documentation under Supported Systems.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 2025-02-11\nVersion: 27419\n\n--- Record 1439 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: New conditional function implemented\nDescription: The conditional function isRegularGroup is implemented to verify whether a given group is a regular user group. It checks consecutively the values of the group attributes supportedOperations and applicationId and returns a Boolean result.  For more information, see Transformation Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 202", ",Neo\nTitle: New conditional function implemented\nDescription: The conditional function isRegularGroup is implemented to verify whether a given group is a regular user group. It checks consecutively the values of the group attributes supportedOperations and applicationId and returns a Boolean result.  For more information, see Transformation Functions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 2025-02-11\nVersion: 27419\n\n--- Record 1440 ---\nComponent: Cloud Identity Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Neo\nTitle: Provisioning sub-attributes of emails attribute\nDescription: Changes in the proxy read transformations of Identity Authentication (version 1 and 2) and Local Identity Directory ensure that Identity Provisioning now reads all sub-attributes of the emails attribute as defined in the SCIM core schema (that is, value, type, primary, display).  For more information, see Identity Authentication (Proxy) and Local Identity Directory (Proxy).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-02-11\nValid as Of: 2025-02-11\nVersion: 27419\n\n", "--- Record 41 ---\nComponent: Joule,SAP BTP Cockpit\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Enhances Navigation in SAP BTP Cockpit\nDescription: Joule now offers navigational scenarios in the BTP cockpit, guiding users to specific pages. Currently, navigation is limited to exporting subaccount users and accessing Cloud Foundry spaces.   This feature streamlines the user experience by providing direct navigation to relevant sections, enhancing efficiency and ease of use. For more information, see Account Administration Using Joule in the Cockpit.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-03\nValid as Of: 2025-06-11\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 42 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Analytical Insights Capability - Support for SAP Datasphere analytic models in an SAP Business Data Cloud formation.\nDescription: Analytic models from SAP Datasphere are now supported by the analytical insights capability in Joule. Your SAP Datasphere system must be part of an SAP Business Data Cloud formation that includes your SAP Analytics Cloud system and Joule.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 43 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Checking sales order fulfillment status in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule allows you to check whether a sales order's fulfillment is on track and identify the issues that block its fulfillment. For each sales order, Joule can tell whether such issues exist in the order processing phase. If yes, you can display issue details, view possible causes and handling suggestions for each issue, and navigate to related apps.  For more information on this capability, see Sales Order Status Check.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Sales\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-30\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 44 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Expiring Prices Handling in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule now enables you to manage expiring prices (stored as condition records for pricing in sales) in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition. With Joule, you can fetch prices that will expire soon, extend their valid-to dates, and adjust their condition amounts or ratios as you need.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Sales\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-30\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 45 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Available in SAP SuccessFactors Mobile apps\nDescription: You can now use Joule, SAP's AI copilot, inSAP SuccessFactors Mobile apps. For more information, see Joule Available in SAP SuccessFactors Mobile\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 46 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Now Available in SAP Digital Manufacturing\nDescription: Joule is now available in SAP Digital Manufacturing for informational use cases. You have conversational access to the product documentation for SAP Digital Manufacturing. Just enter your query or question in plain natural language, and Joule searches the product documentation to find the answer. Joule summarizes the search results in the background. This summarization is then displayed to you as the answer to your question, along with the top three search results. If you select the title link of a result, you're taken directly to the relevant topic on SAP Help Portal.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 47 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Joule Transactional Use Cases are now Enabled for Cash Management Capabilities in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: You can now use Joule to provide comprehensive cash management capabilities, including monitoring bank statements, analyzing cash flow, and initiating bank transfers. This feature is essential for efficiently managing finances, identifying cash shortages, and maintaining a clear overview of financial activities.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 48 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Case Now Supported for Field Logistics in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition\nDescription: The following transactional use case is now supported in Field Logistics for SAP S/4HANA Cloud Private Edition:      Fetch Quantity for a Non-Stock Item    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 49 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Available in SAP SuccessFactors\nDescription: The following Joule use cases are now available in SAP SuccessFactors:", "      Fetch Quantity for a Non-Stock Item    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 49 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Available in SAP SuccessFactors\nDescription: The following Joule use cases are now available in SAP SuccessFactors:      View current roles      View target roles      View offboarding tasks      View enrolled benefits      Explain pay statement      For more information, see SAP SuccessFactors What's New for Joule.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 50 ---\nComponent: Joule\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Use Cases Now Supported in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition\nDescription: Joule now enables you to view business data of the following objects in SAP S/4HANA Cloud Public Edition:  Work Center  Resource    For a list of the supported business objects, their details, and sample requests, see Viewing Business Data.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-05-31\nValid as Of: 2025-05-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 1991 ---\nComponent: SAP Datasphere\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Features for Version 2024.23\nDescription: New and changed features are available for data cataloging, data integration, and data modeling.  For more information, see What's New in SAP Datasphere 2024.23. \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-05\nValid as Of: 2024-11-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1992 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Task Recipients Limited to 100\nDescription: Please note that the task recipients are restricted by SAP Task Center to 100 members, applicable to both users and user groups.  For more information, see Conventions and Technical Restrictions.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-05\nValid as Of: 2024-11-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1993 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Troubleshooting Guide Extended\nDescription: The troubleshooting guide for administrators is extended with details on how to troubleshoot missing tasks.   For more information, see Troubleshooting a Task at SAP Task Center (For Administrators).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-05\nValid as Of: 2024-11-05\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1994 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Pipeline API added.  This pipeline segments data into chunks and generates embeddings, which are multidimensional representations of textual information. The embeddings are stored in a vector database.  For more information, see Create a Document Grounding Pipeline Using the Pipelines API (without Metadata).\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-04\nValid as Of: 2024-11-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1995 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Core\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: A new module has been added to the orchestration system. The grounding module enhances AI processes by integrating external data that is contextually relevant, domain-specific, or real-time. This additional data complements the natural language processing abilities of pretrained models, which are typically based on general information.For more information, see Grounding.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-04\nValid as Of: 2024-11-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1996 ---\nComponent: SAP AI Launchpad\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Generative AI hub\nDescription: Change of the default model from Chat GPT 3.5.  For users with an active Mistral Large deployment, Mistral Large is the default model.  For users without an active Mistral Large deployment, another available model will be selected as the default model.  Users without an active deployment for any other model, should create a new deployment for a model of their choice.  For more information, see Create a Deployment for a Generative AI Model.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-04\nValid as Of: 2024-11-04\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1997 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Changed IP Addresses for SAP Connectivity Service\nDescription: On November 1st, 2024, new IP endpoints will be implemented for the SAP Connectivity service. This change may affect jobs that utilize Cloud Connector and have IP restrictions in place. For the updated list of IP addresses, see Prerequisites.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-11-01\nValid as Of: 2024-11-01\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1998 ---\nComponent: Multitarget Applications for Cloud Foundry\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Removal of MTA module types business-logging and com.sap.business-logging.content\nDescription: The MTA module types business-logging and com.sap.business-logging.content are deprecated and will be removed at the end of 2024 due to the deprecation of an internal mechanism.  If you continue using these module types in your MTA, the deployments will fail with a similar error message: Error merging descriptors: Unsupported module type \"business-logging\" for platform type \"CLOUD-FOUNDRY\".   Action: Migrate to other module types depending on your needs. If you require support, report an incident to component BC-CP-CF-DS.\nAction: Required\nLifecycle: Deprecated\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-10-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1999 ---\nComponent: Authorization and Trust Management Service\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Other\nTitle: Provisioning of Members in the Cloud Foundry Environment (Organizations and and Spaces) Using SAP Cloud Identity Services - Identity Provisioning\nDescription: You can now provision users and roles to Cloud Foundry orgs and spaces using SAP Cloud Identity Services - Identity Provisioning. This improvement enables", ": 2024-10-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 1999 ---\nComponent: Authorization and Trust Management Service\nEnvironment: ABAP,Cloud Foundry,Kyma,Other\nTitle: Provisioning of Members in the Cloud Foundry Environment (Organizations and and Spaces) Using SAP Cloud Identity Services - Identity Provisioning\nDescription: You can now provision users and roles to Cloud Foundry orgs and spaces using SAP Cloud Identity Services - Identity Provisioning. This improvement enables you to centrally manage your platform users from your identity and access management solution. The improvement also helps you to delete the personal data of these users, when they aren't needed anymore.  For more information, see:      SAP BTP Integration Scenario in System Integration Guide for SAP Cloud Identity Services      About User Management in the Cloud Foundry Environment    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-28\nValid as Of: 2024-10-31\nVersion: 2410b\n\n--- Record 2000 ---\nComponent: Availability Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Configure Certificate Expiration and Certificate Chain Validation for AvT Certificate Monitors\nDescription: AvS introduced Certificate type monitors for AvT that can be configured to check certificate expiration and certificate chain validation. For more information, see  ?sap-ot O2O class=\"- topic/xref \" href=\"643030f616404d21babdd9a12e1911b5.xml\" text=\"\" desc=\"\" xtrc=\"xref:6\" xtrf=\"file:/home/builder/src/dita-all/yoe1460360436347/loio922bf2dbe0b646aaaa8cb5e077cfd799_en-US/src/content/localization/en-us/6da9927f396a47609f58c262831b0d9e.xml\" output-class=\"xref\" outputTopicFile=\"file:/home/builder/tp.net.sf.dita-ot/2.3/plugins/com.sap.prd.dita.html5/xsl/sap-html5/sap-html5-table-json.xsl\" ? . Existing evaluations are not affected by the change.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Announcement\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-10-31\nValid as Of: 2024-10-31\nVersion: Cloud\n\n", "--- Record 301 ---\nComponent: SAP Task Center\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Feature  Activity Log\nDescription: You can now view your task's history with the Activity Log in the SAP Task Center Web app.  For more information, see Activity Log, Attachments and Comments.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-14\nValid as Of: 2025-08-14\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 302 ---\nComponent: ABAP Environment\nEnvironment: ABAP\nTitle: Delivering an Add-On Product with the Landscape Portal\nDescription: If you have an SAP Partner Edge Build contract, you can now publish a product as an add-on product. This offers a second delivery option for partners as an alternative to the multitenancy SaaS solution. Your product will appear in the SAP Store, where eligible customers can install it in their own SAP BTP ABAP environment system. The Landscape Portal is used for both, to publish add-on products by partners, and to install them by the customers.  For more information, see New Software Delivery Option \"Add-On Product\".\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: ABAP Environment 2508\n\n--- Record 303 ---\nComponent: Cloud Integration\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: IBM MQ Adapter Supports New Version\nDescription: A new version 1.3.0 of the IBM MQ adapter supports Client Certificate based authentication for JMS Variants.  See: IBM MQ Adapter\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-13\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: 2506\n\n--- Record 304 ---\nComponent: Kyma Runtime\nEnvironment: Kyma\nTitle: API Gateway module: Update to version 3.1.3\nDescription: The new version brings the following changes:      Now, APIRules v1beta1 that are not migrated to version v2 are in the Warning state.    In the controller, the deployed images are now provided using environment variables.  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-12\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 305 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Document Pricing – Do Not Lose Condition Values During Repricing\nDescription: If a price recalculation with type C (Carries out a new pricing, manually entered conditions are retained) was triggered, an automatically determined condition value used to get lost in the following case: The condition appeared twice in the results, one value with control flag A (Adjust for quantity variance) and origin flag A (Automatic pricing) and another value with control flag C (Changed manually) and origin flag C (Manually entered/changed). This issue has been corrected, which can lead to unexpected pricing results if the issue was unnoticed before.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 306 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production - Support More Standard Pricing Routines\nDescription: There are some newly supported pricing requirement formulas:    11 No Material    20 Price Charge    28 No Variant (SA)    29 No Exception 'N'  30 No Exclusion 'V'  35 Plant Info Record  37 Variant  42 Pricing – Normal  57 Not Free Goods w/o return item    Newly supported pricing base value formulas:  23 Preference  25 Cash Discount  44 VAT France  61 Preference  220 Gross Value    See: Supported Standard Pricing Exits.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 307 ---\nComponent: Pricing Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Production – Size Limit for Price Determination Trace\nDescription: Pricing service will stop writing pricing determination traces when an estimated memory size of about 5MB was reached. That should be sufficient for most cases. When the limit is reached, a corresponding info message is added to the trace. SAP can optimize this size limit for support cases and can furthermore limit the pricing determination trace to a list of relevant condition types.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-06-25\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 308 ---\nComponent: Responsibility Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Data Center\nDescription: The Responsibility Management Service is now also available on the Google Cloud Platform in AP30 (Sydney, Australia). See Pricing and Regions Information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-13\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 309 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with Document Grounding\nDescription: The document grounding capability uses information gathered from documents", "30 (Sydney, Australia). See Pricing and Regions Information.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-13\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 309 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Integration with Document Grounding\nDescription: The document grounding capability uses information gathered from documents as a resource for AI tools. By integrating document grounding with SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition, company-specific content stored in public workspaces and knowledge-base articles can be used as a source for AI queries, and provide valuable business-related context.  After completing the configuration steps, company administrators can select which public workspaces will be enabled as AI sources in theAdministration ConsoleArea & Workspace Configuration Workspaces screen.  For more information about the configuration, see Integration with Document Grounding.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-13\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: 2507B\n\n--- Record 310 ---\nComponent: SAP Build Work Zone, advanced edition\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: SCIM DL/Dynamic Distribution List Improvements\nDescription: The per user sync time for both dynamic distribution lists as well as SCIM distribution lists, has been significantly reduced, thus making it much quicker for users to access their workspaces after a sync.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2025-08-13\nValid as Of: 2025-08-13\nVersion: 2507B\n\n", "--- Record 4001 ---\nComponent: Responsibility Management Service\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Service Domains updated\nDescription: We have updated Responsibility Management Service domains. Once you log in with the old URL, you are automatically redirected to the new domain.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-03\nValid as Of: 2023-10-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4002 ---\nComponent: SAP HANA Spatial Services\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry,Kyma\nTitle: nan\nDescription:     Enhancements: Mapping API, Routing API, Geocoding API  Security updates have been implemented.      Bug Fix: Routing API  In Single Routing, the various property would not be correctly applied to single-routing requests for provider Trimble.  In Single Routing, the returned route geometries consisted of improper linestrings for provider Trimble.      Decommissioning: Routing API, Geocoding API  Parameters app_id and app_code for provider Here have been decommissioned. Now, only the parameter api_key is supported.  Routing API  Geocoding API    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2024-01-01\nValid as Of: 2023-10-24\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4003 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Automatic Login with WebdriverIO Tests\nDescription: You can now use the automatic login feature from SAPUI5 when running WebdriverIO tests. See Authentication.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4004 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Failing Job in Case of an Invalid package.json File\nDescription: For a smooth Chromedriver update period, SAP Continuous Integration and Delivery tries to fetch the needed Chromedriver version from the package.json files that are part of the project. If one of these files had an invalid syntax, the connected jobs failed during the Init stage and showed a stack trace instead of a readable error message. Now, these jobs don’t stop in the Init phase anymore and report the invalid package.json file as information only.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4005 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Information about Credential Usage\nDescription: The detail screen of a credential now shows in which jobs or repositories it is being used.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4006 ---\nComponent: Continuous Integration & Delivery\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Transport Request ID in Build Log\nDescription: If in the Release stage of your job, the upload to CTS+ is enabled, the ID of the created transport request is now displayed in the build log again.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: Cloud\n\n--- Record 4007 ---\nComponent: Integration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Integration Assessment: 1.20.*    Increment: 2309  \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: Changed\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: 2309\n\n--- Record 4008 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Extraction Status for Data Extractions\nDescription: Migration Assessment now displays the extraction status of a data extraction. The extraction status designates if the application encountered any warnings or errors during the extraction that might impact future evaluations of the data. If a data extraction finishes with warnings or errors, some data could not be extracted and might even not be used in the scenario evaluation. In these cases, see the extraction log for details and go back to your SAP Process Orchestration System and fix the issues before starting a new extraction.   Note that extraction status is not available for data extractions made before this software update. If you want to see the extraction status of data that was extracted before the update, you must create a new data extraction with the dataset.  See Concepts and Create a Data Extraction Request.\nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: 2309\n\n--- Record 4009 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: New Rules Added\nDescription: The following rules have been added for Migration Assessment:        ReceiverJDBCMessageProtocol: Check if native SQL or raw XML are used on the JDBC receiver.      JDBCLookup: Check if JDBC lookups are using supported JDBC drivers.       \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23", "Title: New Rules Added\nDescription: The following rules have been added for Migration Assessment:        ReceiverJDBCMessageProtocol: Check if native SQL or raw XML are used on the JDBC receiver.      JDBCLookup: Check if JDBC lookups are using supported JDBC drivers.       \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: 2309\n\n--- Record 4010 ---\nComponent: Migration Assessment\nEnvironment: Cloud Foundry\nTitle: Software Version Update\nDescription:     Migration Assessment: 1.21.*      Increment: 2309    \nAction: Info only\nLifecycle: General Availability\nType: New\nLine of Business: Technology\nLatest Revision: 2023-10-23\nValid as Of: 2023-10-23\nVersion: 2309\n\n"], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small"}}, "key": "embeddings_ac6ca4ad927b405912ae31b2c13e44d22f2dd9ebd23f725b82ab703252e3f73d_v2"}